==Strategy==
This stage might look extremely difficult at first, but is actually very simple, requiring only good timing skills. The nasty peons in this level are still relatively tame, and the boss himself, despite his extreme reach (stands at 700, Omni Strike hits up to 1500), cannot push much on his own due to his speed.

The key to clearing Immeasurable Power is in being able to manage the peon waves and keeping Newtone at bay. This can be done using fast cats such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] to quickly activate his attack animation and allow Awakened Bahamut to clear the peons and attack Newtone. [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk Cat]] and [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] can also be spawned in between attacks to stall him further.

Squire Rel and Mr. Angel is just minor inconvenience, they die easily but they might bait your attackers (ex: [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]) into wasting their attack. Li'l Bun Bun die pretty quickly to Fishman Cat. This make Angelic Gory the only threatening peons but your rusher (ex: [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]]) should be enough to severely cribble him.

Any fast [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] rusher, such as [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]] can be used similarly to Awakened Bahamut Cat since they can quickly clear peons before dying, or help chain the boss in tandem with Awakened Bahamut Cat. You can also use nukers such as [[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultimate Thundia β]] or [[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]] to deal insanely high amounts of damage to Newtone between his 10-second attack cycles.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*Fast units such as [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] or [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] can be effectively used to stall, damage or clear peons between Newtone's attacks.
**A level 50 Fishman Cat can kill Li'l Bun Bun in 5 hits, you can also let Li'l  Bun Bun attack Fishman Cat to reset their attacks and kill Li'l Bun Bun quicker.
**[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] can be deploy when you have around 560 cent to bait Newtone and kill first Squire Rel.
*[[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Carpenter Cat]]: An excellent anti-Red/Floating meatshield capable of withstanding an unstrengthened hit from Newtone at Lv.41+ as well as being able to tank the Li'l Bun Bun's hits.
*[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]]: Disposable anti-Red specialist tanker with their Resistance ability giving them extremely high effective health versus [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red enemies]], especially at higher levels, enough to tank at least one Newtone attack, and can more effectively stall with the Resist Slow [[Talents|Talent]], though that isn't particularly necessary.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Its Waves can clear paths for your rushers & nukers and chips Newtone.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Disposable LD anti-Red specialist with [[Massive Damage]] against them. While Courier is unlikely to land more than one or two hits, whatever it dishes out can still chip away at Newtone in between his attacks thanks to its high speed.
*Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Boasting very high damage with his Explosion talent maxed, Bahamut can be used like a generic rusher, however what really sets him apart is the fact that he has enough damage to chain the boss with support from other rushers such as Idi:NX and Bullet Train Cat.
*[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]: Effective answers to the Angelic Gory waves, as both are fast and won't cause you to lose ground to Newtone.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]]: Able to take 12 hits from everything (unfortunately including peons), and can serve as a final line to stall anything in case all other meatshields are one-shot.
*[[882 (Special Cat)|882-2]]: Can interrupt Newtone's Attack Animation to rush down for a prolonged time.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultimate Thundia β]]: Her Ultra Form is a hard counter to this stage only requiring some timing/setup.
**[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]] with Speed Up Talent can be use similarly, although he is more expensive and required Savage Blow to have comparable damage, he is faster.
*[[Count Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Vampiric Yukimura]]: Used to instantly take down the Li'l Bun Bun and initiate more complicated Bahamut chains.
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]]: Very similar to Vampiric Yukimura, they can easily kill Angelic Gory, the most problematic peon in 2 hits at level 41. Their Omni Strike also ensure that they won't miss their attacks.
*[[Mighty Sphinx Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Hyper Battalion Convoys]]: A tanky unit with high speed, he can survive a few good strikes from Newtone. While Newtone can resist Knockback and Weaken due to them lacking Sage Slayer, his attack can still be interrupted by Hyper Battalion Convoys. This can give more breathing room for Awakened Bahamut or other units to aid in chunking Newtone.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Kaza Jizo]]: Very useful against killing the Angelic Gory, and is very cheap and spammable and guranteed to Survive against a lethal hit, which means he can gurantee to get at least 2 hits on the Gory. Since it only takes Jizo around 5 hits at Lvl. 60 to end the 300% magnified Angelic Gory, even with terrible timing you will only need to spawn 2 that will guarantee you a kill.

